"document: which columns hold x and y, how their axes are titled, and which "
"correction turns the raw file into the curve."
msgstr ""
"<code>xyReading</code> tells a client how to read an XY curve (a spectrum) "
"out of a <code>Dataset</code> content resource of a IIIF Presentation 3 "
"document: which columns hold x and y, how their axes are titled, and which "
"correction turns the raw file into the curve."

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:13
msgid "Where it appears"
msgstr "Where it appears"

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:14
msgid ""
"Only on a content resource of type <code>Dataset</code>, usually an "
"annotation body. Any other resource MUST NOT carry it. A document that uses "
"it lists this context first in its <code>@context</code> and the "
"Presentation 3 context last:"
msgstr ""
"Only on a content resource of type <code>Dataset</code>, usually an "
"annotation body. Any other resource MUST NOT carry it. A document that uses "
"it lists this context first in its <code>@context</code> and the "
"Presentation 3 context last:"

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:16
msgid ""
"A document that also declares IIIF Authorization 2.0 services lists the "
"Authorization 2.0 context between the two:"
msgstr ""
"A document that also declares IIIF Authorization 2.0 services lists the "
"Authorization 2.0 context between the two:"

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:18
msgid ""
"The Presentation 2.1 routes carry the same object, with this context before "
"the Presentation 2 context."
msgstr ""
"The Presentation 2.1 routes carry the same object, with this context before "
"the Presentation 2 context."

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:20
msgid "Advisory"
msgstr "Advisory"

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:21
msgid ""
"Clients MAY use <code>xyReading</code> to draw the curve; they SHOULD fall "
"back to their own reading of the file when they do not, and MUST ignore keys"
" they do not know. Every key published is one the ManuSpectrum reader "
"applies."
msgstr ""
"Clients MAY use <code>xyReading</code> to draw the curve; they SHOULD fall "
"back to their own reading of the file when they do not, and MUST ignore keys"
" they do not know. Every key published is one the ManuSpectrum reader "
"applies."

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:23
msgid "Keys"
msgstr "Keys"

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:26
msgid "The type of the object. Required."
msgstr "The type of the object. Required."

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:28
msgid ""
"CSV dialect of the file (CSV on the Web terms): <code>delimiter</code>, "
"<code>headerRowCount</code>, <code>encoding</code>. Given for the files "
"ManuSpectrum writes."
msgstr ""
"CSV dialect of the file (CSV on the Web terms): <code>delimiter</code>, "
"<code>headerRowCount</code>, <code>encoding</code>. Given for the files "
"ManuSpectrum writes."

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:30
msgid ""
"The columns read, in order: <code>index</code> (from 0) and "
"<code>role</code>."
msgstr ""
"The columns read, in order: <code>index</code> (from 0) and "
"<code>role</code>."

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:32
msgid "Zero-based index of a column."
msgstr "Zero-based index of a column."

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:34
msgid ""
"What a column holds: <code id=\"x\">x</code> (the x axis), <code "
"id=\"yLeft\">yLeft</code> and <code id=\"yRight\">yRight</code> (a "
"measurement on the left or right axis), <code "
"id=\"reference\">reference</code> (the white reference), <code "
"id=\"dark\">dark</code> (the dark current), <code "
"id=\"ignore\">ignore</code>."
msgstr ""
"What a column holds: <code id=\"x\">x</code> (the x axis), <code "
"id=\"yLeft\">yLeft</code> and <code id=\"yRight\">yRight</code> (a "
"measurement on the left or right axis), <code "
"id=\"reference\">reference</code> (the white reference), <code "
"id=\"dark\">dark</code> (the dark current), <code "
"id=\"ignore\">ignore</code>."

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:36
msgid ""
"The x axis: <code>label</code> (a IIIF language map) and "
"<code>reversed</code> (true when the axis is drawn from right to left; the "
"rows keep the file's order)."
msgstr ""
"The x axis: <code>label</code> (a IIIF language map) and "
"<code>reversed</code> (true when the axis is drawn from right to left; the "
"rows keep the file's order)."

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:38
msgid ""
"The y axes, in order: <code id=\"axisSide\">axis</code> (<code>left</code> "
"or <code>right</code>) and <code>label</code>."
msgstr ""
"The y axes, in order: <code id=\"axisSide\">axis</code> (<code>left</code> "
"or <code>right</code>) and <code>label</code>."

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:40
msgid "Whether the x axis is drawn from right to left."
msgstr "Whether the x axis is drawn from right to left."

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:42
msgid ""
"How several measurement columns combine: <code>reference-normalize</code> "
"divides the measurement by the reference (see corrections)."
msgstr ""
"How several measurement columns combine: <code>reference-normalize</code> "
"divides the measurement by the reference (see corrections)."

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:44
msgid ""
"The corrections applied, in order. Version 1 knows <code>reference-"
"normalize</code>: <code id=\"expression\">expression</code> <code>(y - dark)"
" / (reference - dark)</code>, <code id=\"darkDefault\">darkDefault</code> "
"the dark value without a dark column (0), <code "
"id=\"epsilon\">epsilon</code> the smallest denominator divided by, and <code"
" id=\"onInvalid\">onInvalid</code> <code>drop-point</code>: a row with a "
"missing value, a non-finite value or a denominator below epsilon is left out"
" of the curve. An empty list says the file already holds the curve."
msgstr ""
"The corrections applied, in order. Version 1 knows <code>reference-"
"normalize</code>: <code id=\"expression\">expression</code> <code>(y - dark)"
" / (reference - dark)</code>, <code id=\"darkDefault\">darkDefault</code> "
"the dark value without a dark column (0), <code "
"id=\"epsilon\">epsilon</code> the smallest denominator divided by, and <code"
" id=\"onInvalid\">onInvalid</code> <code>drop-point</code>: a row with a "
"missing value, a non-finite value or a denominator below epsilon is left out"
" of the curve. An empty list says the file already holds the curve."

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:46
msgid ""
"The raw file the Dataset was derived from (PROV "
"<code>wasDerivedFrom</code>): <code>id</code>, <code>type</code>, "
"<code>format</code>, <code>label</code> and, for a raw text file, its own "
"<code>xyReading</code> (columns and corrections)."
msgstr ""
"The raw file the Dataset was derived from (PROV "
"<code>wasDerivedFrom</code>): <code>id</code>, <code>type</code>, "
"<code>format</code>, <code>label</code> and, for a raw text file, its own "
"<code>xyReading</code> (columns and corrections)."

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:49
msgid ""
"The Dataset is never decimated, whatever its size. mirador-xyviewer does not"
" plot a Dataset larger than 5 MB; such a file still plots in the "
"ManuSpectrum Explorer."
msgstr ""
"The Dataset is never decimated, whatever its size. mirador-xyviewer does not"
" plot a Dataset larger than 5 MB; such a file still plots in the "
"ManuSpectrum Explorer."

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:51
msgid "Restricted data (IIIF Authorization)"
msgstr "Restricted data (IIIF Authorization)"

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:52
msgid ""
"Open data needs no credential. A restricted spectrum, annotation or content "
"state answers <code>401</code> with a description that names the IIIF "
"Authorization services; annotation pages and collections are never refused: "
"they list what the reader may see and declare the same services."
msgstr ""
"Open data needs no credential. A restricted spectrum, annotation or content "
"state answers <code>401</code> with a description that names the IIIF "
"Authorization services; annotation pages and collections are never refused: "
"they list what the reader may see and declare the same services."

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:54
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Login: the viewer opens <a href=\"%(login_url)s\">%(login_url)s</a> in a new"
" window (IIIF Auth 1.0 <code>login</code> profile, Auth 2.0 "
"<code>active</code> profile). The reader signs in to ManuSpectrum there; the"
" window then says so and can be closed."
msgstr ""
"Login: the viewer opens <a href=\"%(login_url)s\">%(login_url)s</a> in a new"
" window (IIIF Auth 1.0 <code>login</code> profile, Auth 2.0 "
"<code>active</code> profile). The reader signs in to ManuSpectrum there; the"
" window then says so and can be closed."

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:55
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Token: the viewer loads <code>%(token1_url)s</code> (Auth 1.0) or "
"<code>%(token2_url)s</code> (Auth 2.0) in a hidden frame with its "
"<code>messageId</code> and <code>origin</code>, and receives an access token"
" valid %(token_minutes)s minutes for that origin only. It sends it as "
"<code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;</code> to the <code>/iiif/</code> "
"read routes; the Auth 2.0 probe service of a spectrum says whether that "
"token opens it."
msgstr ""
"Token: the viewer loads <code>%(token1_url)s</code> (Auth 1.0) or "
"<code>%(token2_url)s</code> (Auth 2.0) in a hidden frame with its "
"<code>messageId</code> and <code>origin</code>, and receives an access token"
" valid %(token_minutes)s minutes for that origin only. It sends it as "
"<code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;</code> to the <code>/iiif/</code> "
"read routes; the Auth 2.0 probe service of a spectrum says whether that "
"token opens it."

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:56
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Logout: opening <a href=\"%(logout_url)s\">%(logout_url)s</a> in a tab (an "
"HTTP GET, as IIIF Auth 1.0 defines it) ends every token of the session; "
"signing out of ManuSpectrum does too. The ManuSpectrum session itself stays "
"open."
msgstr ""
"Logout: opening <a href=\"%(logout_url)s\">%(logout_url)s</a> in a tab (an "
"HTTP GET, as IIIF Auth 1.0 defines it) ends every token of the session; "
"signing out of ManuSpectrum does too. The ManuSpectrum session itself stays "
"open."

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:58
msgid ""
"The token only reads: it opens the <code>/iiif/</code> routes and nothing "
"else, and it is not an API credential. Tokens go only to this site and to "
"the viewers its administrators trust; any other origin receives "
"<code>invalidOrigin</code>. A Bearer token that is not a IIIF token of this "
"site is refused."
msgstr ""
"The token only reads: it opens the <code>/iiif/</code> routes and nothing "
"else, and it is not an API credential. Tokens go only to this site and to "
"the viewers its administrators trust; any other origin receives "
"<code>invalidOrigin</code>. A Bearer token that is not a IIIF token of this "
"site is refused."

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:59
msgid "Known limits"
msgstr "Known limits"

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:61
msgid ""
"HTTPS is required: the access cookie is <code>Secure; SameSite=None</code>, "
"and a browser does not keep it on a plain HTTP site."
msgstr ""
"HTTPS is required: the access cookie is <code>Secure; SameSite=None</code>, "
"and a browser does not keep it on a plain HTTP site."

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:62
msgid ""
"Third-party cookies: the token frame belongs to this site inside the "
"viewer's page. Chrome sends the cookie; Safari (Intelligent Tracking "
"Prevention) and Firefox (Total Cookie Protection) may block it, and the "
"viewer then keeps asking to sign in. Use Chrome, a viewer served from this "
"site, or allow this site's cookies in the browser."
msgstr ""
"Third-party cookies: the token frame belongs to this site inside the "
"viewer's page. Chrome sends the cookie; Safari (Intelligent Tracking "
"Prevention) and Firefox (Total Cookie Protection) may block it, and the "
"viewer then keeps asking to sign in. Use Chrome, a viewer served from this "
"site, or allow this site's cookies in the browser."

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:63
msgid ""
"The ManuSpectrum session cookie is <code>SameSite=Strict</code>: the login "
"window opened from another site may ask to sign in again even when another "
"tab is already signed in."
msgstr ""
"The ManuSpectrum session cookie is <code>SameSite=Strict</code>: the login "
"window opened from another site may ask to sign in again even when another "
"tab is already signed in."

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:64
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The viewer renews its token silently while the access cookie lives: at most "
"%(cookie_hours)s hours, and never longer than the ManuSpectrum session."
msgstr ""
"The viewer renews its token silently while the access cookie lives: at most "
"%(cookie_hours)s hours, and never longer than the ManuSpectrum session."

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:67
msgid "Versions"
msgstr "Versions"

#: templates/iiif/xy_reading_1.htm:68
msgid ""
"The major version is in the path of the context (<code>/1</code>). Version 1"
" only gains optional keys; a change of meaning would be version 2, at a new "
"path."
msgstr ""
"The major version is in the path of the context (<code>/1</code>). Version 1"
" only gains optional keys; a change of meaning would be version 2, at a new "
